   "rationale": "Directly related to the #' divergence tracked in fe's own manifest (reader-sharp-quote-identity): kg's `function` only coincidentally behaves right for `(function car)` used as a plain reference to a primitive, because evaluating `car` happens to yield the same primitive object either way for a *primitive*; it clearly diverges once the return value itself is compared (a primitive object vs. the symbol car), which is exactly what this case shows. Not fixed in this slice; a real `function` needs the reader-level `#'` fix that lives in fe's manifest, so this entry does not name its own phase.",
